§ `Part IV - Residential tenancy agreements`

§§ `Division 1 - Rent and security bonds`

DECLARE `monetary amount demanded` HAS
    `the amount is rent` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the amount is a security bond` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the amount is option consideration not exceeding the prescribed amount` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the option is exercised` IS A BOOLEAN
    `upon the option being exercised the amount is refunded in cash or applied towards the rent` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the option is refused` IS A BOOLEAN
    `upon the option being refused the amount is refunded within 7 days in cash, by electronic means or in a prescribed way` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the lessor is authorised by any other provision of this Act to require or receive the amount` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the amount is a payment of a prescribed class` IS A BOOLEAN

DECLARE `tenancy advertisement` HAS
    `the advertisement states a fixed amount of rent` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the advertisement states that rent is calculated by reference to the tenant's income` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the advertisement is a sign at or near the premises that does not state an amount of rent` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a person is invited to offer a rent higher than the advertised amount` IS A BOOLEAN

DECLARE `rent demand` HAS
    `the demand is made before or during the first 2 weeks of the tenancy` IS A BOOLEAN
    `weeks of rent demanded` IS A NUMBER
    `the demand is the first payment of rent` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the period of the tenancy in respect of which any previous payment has been made has elapsed` IS A BOOLEAN

DECLARE `security bond demand` HAS
    `more than one security bond is required or received` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the amount is received in instalments` IS A BOOLEAN
    `security bond amount` IS A NUMBER
    `4 weeks rent` IS A NUMBER
    `the tenant is permitted to keep a pet at the premises` IS A BOOLEAN
    `prescribed pet bond amount` IS A NUMBER
    `the weekly rate of rent exceeds the prescribed amount` IS A BOOLEAN
    `further payment is required from a remaining tenant to cover disposal of a former tenant's portion under section 17B(3)` IS A BOOLEAN

§§§ `27. Restriction on consideration for tenancy agreement`

-- s.27(2)(a): option consideration, refunded or applied as required.

GIVEN amount IS A `monetary amount demanded`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the amount is permitted option consideration` IF
        amount's `the amount is option consideration not exceeding the prescribed amount`
    AND (
            (
                amount's `the option is exercised`
            AND amount's `upon the option being exercised the amount is refunded in cash or applied towards the rent`
            )
        OR  (
                amount's `the option is refused`
            AND amount's `upon the option being refused the amount is refunded within 7 days in cash, by electronic means or in a prescribed way`
            )
        )

-- s.27(1): a person must not require or receive from a tenant any
-- monetary amount other than rent and a security bond, subject to s.27(2).

@ref Residential Tenancies Act 1987 (WA) s.27
@export Decide whether a monetary amount required or received from a tenant is permitted under s.27
GIVEN amount IS A `monetary amount demanded` @desc The amount: whether it is rent, a security bond, option consideration (not exceeding the prescribed amount, with the matching refund or rent-application limb), an amount the lessor is authorised by another provision of this Act to require or receive, or a prescribed class of payment.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the consideration is permitted` IF
        amount's `the amount is rent`
    OR  amount's `the amount is a security bond`
    OR  `the amount is permitted option consideration` amount
    OR  amount's `the lessor is authorised by any other provision of this Act to require or receive the amount`
    OR  amount's `the amount is a payment of a prescribed class`

§§§ `27AA. Residential tenancy must be offered for rent at a fixed amount`

GIVEN advertisement IS A `tenancy advertisement`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 27AA(2) sign exception applies` IF
    advertisement's `the advertisement is a sign at or near the premises that does not state an amount of rent`

@ref Residential Tenancies Act 1987 (WA) s.27AA
@export Decide whether an advertisement or offer of a residential tenancy complies with s.27AA(1)
GIVEN advertisement IS A `tenancy advertisement` @desc The advertisement or offer: whether it states a fixed rent, states that rent is calculated by reference to the tenant's income, is a sign at or near the premises that does not state an amount of rent, and whether anyone is invited to offer a rent higher than advertised.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the advertisement complies with section 27AA(1)` IF
        `section 27AA(2) sign exception applies` advertisement
    OR  advertisement's `the advertisement states a fixed amount of rent`
    OR  advertisement's `the advertisement states that rent is calculated by reference to the tenant's income`

GIVEN advertisement IS A `tenancy advertisement`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person solicits a rent higher than advertised` IF
    advertisement's `a person is invited to offer a rent higher than the advertised amount`

§§§ `28. Rent in advance`

GIVEN demand IS A `rent demand`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 28(1) is contravened` IF
        demand's `the demand is made before or during the first 2 weeks of the tenancy`
    AND demand's `weeks of rent demanded` GREATER THAN 2

GIVEN demand IS A `rent demand`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 28(2) is contravened` IF
        NOT demand's `the demand is the first payment of rent`
    AND (
            NOT demand's `the period of the tenancy in respect of which any previous payment has been made has elapsed`
        OR  demand's `weeks of rent demanded` GREATER THAN 2
        )

@ref Residential Tenancies Act 1987 (WA) s.28
@export Decide whether a rent-in-advance requirement is prohibited by s.28
GIVEN demand IS A `rent demand` @desc The rent demand: whether it is made before or during the first 2 weeks of the tenancy; weeks of rent demanded (2 means 2 weeks' rent); whether it is the first payment; and whether the period covered by any previous payment has elapsed.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the rent in advance requirement is prohibited` IF
        `section 28(1) is contravened` demand
    OR  `section 28(2) is contravened` demand

§§§ `29. Security bonds`

GIVEN demand IS A `security bond demand`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 29(1)(a) is contravened` IF
        demand's `more than one security bond is required or received`
    AND NOT demand's `the amount is received in instalments`
    AND NOT demand's `further payment is required from a remaining tenant to cover disposal of a former tenant's portion under section 17B(3)`

GIVEN demand IS A `security bond demand`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the permitted security bond aggregate` IS
    IF demand's `the tenant is permitted to keep a pet at the premises`
    THEN demand's `4 weeks rent` PLUS demand's `prescribed pet bond amount`
    ELSE demand's `4 weeks rent`

GIVEN demand IS A `security bond demand`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 29(1)(b) is contravened` IF
        NOT demand's `the weekly rate of rent exceeds the prescribed amount`
    AND demand's `security bond amount` GREATER THAN `the permitted security bond aggregate` demand

@ref Residential Tenancies Act 1987 (WA) s.29
@export Decide whether a security bond required or received is prohibited by s.29(1)
GIVEN demand IS A `security bond demand` @desc The bond demand. Amounts in the same currency unit (for example AUD). Fields: more than one bond required or received; received in instalments; security bond amount; 4 weeks' rent; pet permitted and the prescribed pet-bond amount; whether weekly rent exceeds the prescribed amount (which switches off the 4-week cap); and whether the extra amount is a remaining tenant covering a former tenant's portion under s.17B(3).
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the security bond is prohibited` IF
        `section 29(1)(a) is contravened` demand
    OR  `section 29(1)(b) is contravened` demand

DECLARE `bond actor` IS ONE OF
    `the person who receives a security bond`

DECLARE `bond action` IS ONE OF
    `pay the bond to the bond administrator`

-- s.29(4)(b): pay the bond to the bond administrator as soon as
-- practicable, and in any event within 14 days after the day received.

GIVEN `the person has received a security bond` IS A BOOLEAN @desc TRUE once a person has received a security bond paid in relation to a residential tenancy agreement.
GIVETH A DEONTIC `bond actor` `bond action`
DECIDE `the security bond lodgement obligation` IS
    IF `the person has received a security bond`
    THEN
        PARTY `the person who receives a security bond`
        MUST `pay the bond to the bond administrator`
        WITHIN 14
        HENCE FULFILLED
        LEST BREACH BY `the person who receives a security bond` BECAUSE "bond not paid to the bond administrator within 14 days after the day on which the person received the bond (s.29(4)(b))"
    ELSE FULFILLED

DECLARE `rent increase notice` HAS
    `rent is calculated by reference to the tenant's income` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the notice is in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the notice is in the approved form` IS A BOOLEAN
    `days after the notice is given until the increase is payable` IS A NUMBER
    `months after commencement or last increase until the increase is payable` IS A NUMBER
    `the tenancy is for a fixed term during its currency` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the amount of the increase or the method of calculating it is set out in the agreement` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the right to increase is excluded or limited by agreement` IS A BOOLEAN

§§§ `30. Variation of rent (except where calculated by reference to tenant's income)`

@ref Residential Tenancies Act 1987 (WA) s.30
@export Decide whether a rent increase under s.30 is permitted
GIVEN notice IS A `rent increase notice` @desc The proposed increase. Set rent is calculated by reference to the tenant's income to TRUE to send the matter to s.31A instead. Days after notice until payable must be at least 60; months after commencement or last increase until payable must be at least 12. For a fixed-term tenancy during its currency the amount or method of increase must be set out in the agreement. The right may also be excluded or limited by agreement.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the rent increase is permitted` IF
        NOT notice's `rent is calculated by reference to the tenant's income`
    AND notice's `the notice is in writing`
    AND notice's `the notice is in the approved form`
    AND notice's `days after the notice is given until the increase is payable` AT LEAST 60
    AND notice's `months after commencement or last increase until the increase is payable` AT LEAST 12
    AND (
            NOT notice's `the tenancy is for a fixed term during its currency`
        OR  notice's `the amount of the increase or the method of calculating it is set out in the agreement`
        )
    AND NOT notice's `the right to increase is excluded or limited by agreement`

DECLARE `rent calculation method notice` HAS
    `rent is calculated by reference to the tenant's income` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the notice is in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the notice is in the approved form` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the notice specifies the change to the method` IS A BOOLEAN
    `days after the notice is given until the change takes effect` IS A NUMBER
    `months after commencement or last change until the change takes effect` IS A NUMBER

§§§ `31A. Variation of rent where calculated by reference to tenant's income`

@ref Residential Tenancies Act 1987 (WA) s.31A
@export Decide whether a change to the income-based rent calculation method is permitted under s.31A
GIVEN notice IS A `rent calculation method notice` @desc A proposed change to the method by which rent is calculated by reference to the tenant's income. The notice must be in writing, in the approved form, specify the change, take effect at least 60 days after it is given, and at least 12 months after commencement or the last such change.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the rent calculation method change is permitted` IF
        notice's `rent is calculated by reference to the tenant's income`
    AND notice's `the notice is in writing`
    AND notice's `the notice is in the approved form`
    AND notice's `the notice specifies the change to the method`
    AND notice's `days after the notice is given until the change takes effect` AT LEAST 60
    AND notice's `months after commencement or last change until the change takes effect` AT LEAST 12

DECLARE `agreement pair` HAS
    `the lessor is the same under both agreements` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the tenant is the same under both agreements` IS A BOOLEAN
    `at least 1 cotenant is the same under both agreements` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the agreements are for the same residential premises` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the continuing agreement starts immediately after the end of the term of the existing agreement` IS A BOOLEAN

§§§ `31B. When residential tenancy agreement is continuation of existing residential tenancy agreement`

GIVEN pair IS A `agreement pair`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the agreements are between the same parties` IF
        pair's `the lessor is the same under both agreements`
    AND (
            pair's `the tenant is the same under both agreements`
        OR  pair's `at least 1 cotenant is the same under both agreements`
        )

@ref Residential Tenancies Act 1987 (WA) s.31B
@export Decide whether a later residential tenancy agreement is taken to be a continuation of an earlier one under s.31B
GIVEN pair IS A `agreement pair` @desc Two agreements compared for s.31B continuation: same lessor; same tenant or at least one same cotenant; same residential premises; and the continuing agreement starts immediately after the end of the existing agreement's term.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the continuing agreement is taken to be a continuation of the existing agreement` IF
        `the agreements are between the same parties` pair
    AND pair's `the agreements are for the same residential premises`
    AND pair's `the continuing agreement starts immediately after the end of the term of the existing agreement`

§§ `Fixtures`

`rent only` MEANS `monetary amount demanded` WITH
    `the amount is rent` IS TRUE,
    `the amount is a security bond` IS FALSE,
    `the amount is option consideration not exceeding the prescribed amount` IS FALSE,
    `the option is exercised` IS FALSE,
    `upon the option being exercised the amount is refunded in cash or applied towards the rent` IS FALSE,
    `the option is refused` IS FALSE,
    `upon the option being refused the amount is refunded within 7 days in cash, by electronic means or in a prescribed way` IS FALSE,
    `the lessor is authorised by any other provision of this Act to require or receive the amount` IS FALSE,
    `the amount is a payment of a prescribed class` IS FALSE

`key money` MEANS `monetary amount demanded` WITH
    `the amount is rent` IS FALSE,
    `the amount is a security bond` IS FALSE,
    `the amount is option consideration not exceeding the prescribed amount` IS FALSE,
    `the option is exercised` IS FALSE,
    `upon the option being exercised the amount is refunded in cash or applied towards the rent` IS FALSE,
    `the option is refused` IS FALSE,
    `upon the option being refused the amount is refunded within 7 days in cash, by electronic means or in a prescribed way` IS FALSE,
    `the lessor is authorised by any other provision of this Act to require or receive the amount` IS FALSE,
    `the amount is a payment of a prescribed class` IS FALSE

`fixed rent advertisement` MEANS `tenancy advertisement` WITH
    `the advertisement states a fixed amount of rent` IS TRUE,
    `the advertisement states that rent is calculated by reference to the tenant's income` IS FALSE,
    `the advertisement is a sign at or near the premises that does not state an amount of rent` IS FALSE,
    `a person is invited to offer a rent higher than the advertised amount` IS FALSE

`rental bidding invitation` MEANS `tenancy advertisement` WITH
    `the advertisement states a fixed amount of rent` IS TRUE,
    `the advertisement states that rent is calculated by reference to the tenant's income` IS FALSE,
    `the advertisement is a sign at or near the premises that does not state an amount of rent` IS FALSE,
    `a person is invited to offer a rent higher than the advertised amount` IS TRUE

`first two weeks three weeks rent` MEANS `rent demand` WITH
    `the demand is made before or during the first 2 weeks of the tenancy` IS TRUE,
    `weeks of rent demanded` IS 3,
    `the demand is the first payment of rent` IS TRUE,
    `the period of the tenancy in respect of which any previous payment has been made has elapsed` IS TRUE

`lawful first two weeks rent` MEANS `rent demand` WITH
    `the demand is made before or during the first 2 weeks of the tenancy` IS TRUE,
    `weeks of rent demanded` IS 2,
    `the demand is the first payment of rent` IS TRUE,
    `the period of the tenancy in respect of which any previous payment has been made has elapsed` IS TRUE

`five weeks bond no pet` MEANS `security bond demand` WITH
    `more than one security bond is required or received` IS FALSE,
    `the amount is received in instalments` IS FALSE,
    `security bond amount` IS 2500,
    `4 weeks rent` IS 2000,
    `the tenant is permitted to keep a pet at the premises` IS FALSE,
    `prescribed pet bond amount` IS 0,
    `the weekly rate of rent exceeds the prescribed amount` IS FALSE,
    `further payment is required from a remaining tenant to cover disposal of a former tenant's portion under section 17B(3)` IS FALSE

`four weeks bond no pet` MEANS `security bond demand` WITH
    `more than one security bond is required or received` IS FALSE,
    `the amount is received in instalments` IS FALSE,
    `security bond amount` IS 2000,
    `4 weeks rent` IS 2000,
    `the tenant is permitted to keep a pet at the premises` IS FALSE,
    `prescribed pet bond amount` IS 0,
    `the weekly rate of rent exceeds the prescribed amount` IS FALSE,
    `further payment is required from a remaining tenant to cover disposal of a former tenant's portion under section 17B(3)` IS FALSE

`valid s.30 increase` MEANS `rent increase notice` WITH
    `rent is calculated by reference to the tenant's income` IS FALSE,
    `the notice is in writing` IS TRUE,
    `the notice is in the approved form` IS TRUE,
    `days after the notice is given until the increase is payable` IS 60,
    `months after commencement or last increase until the increase is payable` IS 12,
    `the tenancy is for a fixed term during its currency` IS FALSE,
    `the amount of the increase or the method of calculating it is set out in the agreement` IS FALSE,
    `the right to increase is excluded or limited by agreement` IS FALSE

`fixed term increase not in agreement` MEANS `rent increase notice` WITH
    `rent is calculated by reference to the tenant's income` IS FALSE,
    `the notice is in writing` IS TRUE,
    `the notice is in the approved form` IS TRUE,
    `days after the notice is given until the increase is payable` IS 60,
    `months after commencement or last increase until the increase is payable` IS 12,
    `the tenancy is for a fixed term during its currency` IS TRUE,
    `the amount of the increase or the method of calculating it is set out in the agreement` IS FALSE,
    `the right to increase is excluded or limited by agreement` IS FALSE

#EVAL `the consideration is permitted` `rent only`
#EVAL `the consideration is permitted` `key money`
#EVAL `the advertisement complies with section 27AA(1)` `fixed rent advertisement`
#EVAL `the person solicits a rent higher than advertised` `rental bidding invitation`
#EVAL `the rent in advance requirement is prohibited` `first two weeks three weeks rent`
#EVAL `the rent in advance requirement is prohibited` `lawful first two weeks rent`
#EVAL `the security bond is prohibited` `five weeks bond no pet`
#EVAL `the security bond is prohibited` `four weeks bond no pet`
#EVAL `the rent increase is permitted` `valid s.30 increase`
#EVAL `the rent increase is permitted` `fixed term increase not in agreement`
#ASSERT `the consideration is permitted` `rent only` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the consideration is permitted` `key money` EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `the rent in advance requirement is prohibited` `first two weeks three weeks rent` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the rent in advance requirement is prohibited` `lawful first two weeks rent` EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `the security bond is prohibited` `five weeks bond no pet` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the security bond is prohibited` `four weeks bond no pet` EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `the rent increase is permitted` `valid s.30 increase` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the rent increase is permitted` `fixed term increase not in agreement` EQUALS FALSE

`renewal of the same tenancy` MEANS `agreement pair` WITH
    `the lessor is the same under both agreements` IS TRUE,
    `the tenant is the same under both agreements` IS TRUE,
    `at least 1 cotenant is the same under both agreements` IS FALSE,
    `the agreements are for the same residential premises` IS TRUE,
    `the continuing agreement starts immediately after the end of the term of the existing agreement` IS TRUE

#EVAL `the continuing agreement is taken to be a continuation of the existing agreement` `renewal of the same tenancy`
#ASSERT `the continuing agreement is taken to be a continuation of the existing agreement` `renewal of the same tenancy` EQUALS TRUE

#TRACE `the security bond lodgement obligation` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the person who receives a security bond` DOES `pay the bond to the bond administrator` AT 10

#TRACE `the security bond lodgement obligation` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the person who receives a security bond` DOES `pay the bond to the bond administrator` AT 20
